<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prasutagus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 60</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prasutagus was king of the Iceni of East Anglia, who ruled as a client of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> after the conquest of 43. On his death around 60 he left half his kingdom to the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a> and half to his daughters, hoping to protect his family. Roman officials instead seized his realm and abused his widow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boudica">Boudica</a> and their daughters, provoking her revolt.</p></div>
